  "verbalization": "Isomaltopaeoniflorin is implicated in the biological activity of SNU1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Isomaltopaeoniflorin acts as a target for MIP, which in turn is a target of (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, and also of Sansalvamide A. Both of these compounds are ultimately linked to SNU1, indicating a potential pathway where Isomaltopaeoniflorin may influence SNU1 through these intermediates. The shared target of MIP and Sansalvamide A to SNU1 suggests a possible functional relationship, possibly involving common downstream effects or signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of MIP and its derivatives in mediating the interaction between Isomaltopaeoniflorin and SNU1, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
